    "why_parked": "The takes recorded for this kind have been read once and the unit is not being asked again for it. What is kept: the byte closes a loop, and on the one type read clean the second pass stands among the strongest features from 95 up. What is given up is a law in the byte, because the stage these runs were made for places copies and does not weigh them, and two of the three types it was to be set on were walked with a chain in front of the delay that the reading never got past. Since parking, the one booking it ended with was run: 04 00's tail at 34 and 64 of `Dly Fb`. What came back is under `the_round_that_read_the_tail`. It is not the loop's decay -- every band the stage fitted fell its twenty decibels inside one pass -- so it answers neither reading, and the field that carried the booking now carries the observable that would.",
    "what_would_reopen": {
      "observable": "How much quieter each copy of a struck note is than the copy before it, round 04 00's loop with its compressor, overdrive and chorus switched out as they were for the walk, at settings 34 and 64 of `Dly Fb`.",
      "predicts": {
        "a loop gain straight in the byte": "5.95 dB a pass at 64 and 11.45 at 34",
        "the loop-gain readout of the phaser's resonance byte (0120-the-resonance-byte-closes-a-loop)": "8.64 dB a pass at 64 and 15.05 at 34"
      },
      "divergence": "2.7 dB a pass at 64 and 3.6 at 34.",
      "sensitivity_here": "None measured: no record of this archive carries the level of one copy against the copy before it, so there is no repeat of that quantity to take a floor from.",
      "margin": null,
      "why_not_separable": "No stage of this archive publishes the level of one copy against another. `decay` integrates from the note's onset and, on this type, finished inside the first pass; `efx-time` places copies and reports how far each stands out of a cepstrum, which is not a level. So there is no measured sensitivity to set the divergence against, and a margin computed against a figure for a different quantity is what this booking was replacing. The condition is a reading that weighs successive passes of a known delay -- a stage change, not a run -- and it is named here rather than queued.",
      "run": null
    }
  },
  "claim": "The byte printed `Dly Fb` closes a loop around the delay, on the one type whose delay was read clear of the rest of its chain: 04 00's copy of the note at 300.0 ms is read at every setting, and a second copy at twice that stands among the three strongest features of every take at 95 and 127 and of none at 0, 32 or 34. How much of the return goes round is not something this stage reads at any setting -- it places a copy and does not weigh one -- and on the other two types walked at five settings the delay was not among the three strongest features of any take, so no law in the byte is set for feedback and none is carried to another type.",
